-- Every keyword skill KEYWORD_NAMES (engine/script-schema.ts) lists, in that
-- order. TAKES is the arity KeywordSkill (engine/types.ts) carries and
-- keywordOf (engine/cards.ts) reads back; scripts/verify/rulesets.ts checks
-- both against this file. text: is the glossary's meaning line, verbatim
-- (src/lib/arena/glossary.ts) — /arena/rules/keywords renders it from here
-- rather than from glossary.ts since #163, and scripts/verify/game-page.ts
-- holds the two equal so the page and the record cannot quietly disagree.
--
-- Fifteen HOOK bodies over fourteen keywords, written by Stage 7's four hook
-- groups (#154-#157) against the contract #153 built: [Field]'s onEnter,
-- [Indestructible]'s koByEffect, [Barrier]'s chooseable, [Deflect]'s
-- counterWindow, [Servant]'s attrBonus and activeStep, [Energy-Exhaust]'s
-- chargeLimit, [Unique]'s playRefused, [Heroic]/[Villainous]'s afterSkill,
-- [Critical]/[Strike]/[Victory Strike]'s beforeDamage and [Revenge]/
-- [Attack]'s battleEnd. Every other keyword's
-- own moments are still the engine's, and each one's trailing comment says
-- which group looked at it and why it is deferred — the header used to say
-- "no HOOK bodies yet", which stopped being true at #154 and was found by
-- #166's pre-flip review.
--
-- Fourteen DO bodies, the whole-keyword activations that are no hook at all
-- (docs/arena-ruleset-spec.md §4.4): [Overlord], [Evolve], [Union],
-- [Successor], [Arrival], [Aegis], [Wish] and [Awaken] are moves (`offer:`),
-- each offered as an [Activate: Main] — [Arrival] and [Aegis] an [Activate:
-- Battle], [Wish] and [Awaken] both — line with its own REFUSE and menu
-- words ([Wish] and [Awaken] with an AFTER as well), and [Offering],
-- [Z-Stack], [Revive], [Alliance], [Revenge] and [Attack] answer a moment
-- (`at:`), pended like an [Auto] — [Alliance] running its printed effect
-- where its DO says (`printedEffect`), the last two with an empty DO,
-- announced as the legacy engine announces them, their effect a battleEnd
-- HOOK. 9-1-4 immunity printed as a [Permanent] is no keyword at all and is
-- read beside the other statics (`vm/effects.ts`, #154). The others of that shape —
-- [Rejuvenate], [Z-Awaken], [Over Realm], [Swap] … — are still to write the
-- same way, each one's trailing comment saying what it is missing.
-- [Spirit Boost] needs no body: it is a price (costs.rules' spiritBoost).

-- 22-2
DEFINE KEYWORD Awaken
  TAKES (surge: boolean)
  text: "A Leader's own skill. Meet the printed condition, pay the cost, carry out the effect, then flip the Leader onto its awakened side. [Awaken: Surge] is the same skill under another name, and card text saying “[Awaken] skills” means both."
  -- #156: [Wish]'s body under its own name (22-2-4 and 22-25-4 are the same
  -- rule) — a move offered at the Main Phase and at the combo prompt from a
  -- face-up Leader that prints an awakened side, while the printed condition
  -- (the record's hoisted price condition) holds; the line's effect runs, and
  -- `AFTER` flips the Leader once it has, even when the effect stopped to ask
  -- something. [Awaken: Surge] is the same move: `surge` changes nothing the
  -- engine does, on either engine, and the menu says "Awaken" for both.
  offer: "activate:main/battle"
  REFUSE zone(area: leader) UNLESS count([self] IN you.leader) >= 1
  REFUSE other(detail: "the Leader is already awakened") UNLESS NOT leaderFlipped()
  REFUSE other(detail: "the Leader has no awakened side") UNLESS leaderMatches(filter: "card", back: true)
  label: "Awaken: {card} → {back}"
  DO {}
  AFTER {
    flip(target: [self])
  }

-- 22-25
DEFINE KEYWORD Wish
  TAKES ()
  text: "The same shape as [Awaken]: a condition, an effect, and then the Leader is flipped over."
  -- #155: a move, offered at the Main Phase and at the combo prompt from a
  -- face-up Leader that prints an awakened side, while the printed condition
  -- holds (the record hoists it into the line's price, 9-1-3). The effect is
  -- the line's own; the flip is the keyword's, and comes after it (`AFTER`,
  -- 22-25-4) even when the effect stops to ask something — the legacy engine
  -- queues it ahead for the same reason. [Awaken] (22-2) is the same body,
  -- declared by #156.
  offer: "activate:main/battle"
  REFUSE zone(area: leader) UNLESS count([self] IN you.leader) >= 1
  REFUSE other(detail: "the Leader is already awakened") UNLESS NOT leaderFlipped()
  REFUSE other(detail: "the Leader has no awakened side") UNLESS leaderMatches(filter: "card", back: true)
  label: "Wish: {card} → {back}"
  DO {}
  AFTER {
    flip(target: [self])
  }

-- 22-3
DEFINE KEYWORD Field
  TAKES ()
  text: "An Extra Card that stays on the table in Active Mode instead of going to the Drop Area. Its other skills work from there, and playing another [Field] Extra drops the one already out."
  HOOK onEnter {
    choose(sel: UP TO 1 "Extra Card with [Field]" IN you.battle otherThanSelf, as: "t")
    moveTo(target: $t, to: drop)
  }

-- 22-4
DEFINE KEYWORD Blocker
  TAKES ()
  text: "When one of your other cards is attacked, switch this card to Rest Mode to become the guard card instead."
  -- Stage 7 (#153–#157)

-- 22-6
DEFINE KEYWORD Critical
  TAKES ()
  text: "Life damage this card deals by attacking goes to the opponent's Drop Area instead of their hand."
  -- #156: read as the attacker's damage lands (`beforeDamage`, a query hook
  -- so it changes this damage rather than a later one): the life cards go
  -- to the Drop face up, and "when your life is placed in your Drop" hears
  -- the move. Battle damage only, as on the legacy engine.
  HOOK beforeDamage {
    battleDamage(to: drop)
  }

-- 22-7
DEFINE KEYWORD Strike
  TAKES (x: number)
  text: "When this card would deal less than X life damage by attacking, it deals X instead — 2, 3 or 4."
  -- #156: the same hook as [Critical]: X life damage to a Leader, and X
  -- markers off a Unison guard (13-5-2-2), as on the legacy engine.
  HOOK beforeDamage {
    battleDamage(atLeast: $x)
  }

-- 22-8
DEFINE KEYWORD Attack
  TAKES (x: number)
  text: "When this card attacks, it switches back to Active Mode at the end of the battle — X−1 times a turn."
  -- #156: two halves, as the legacy engine has them. The line answers
  -- `attacks` (`at:`), so it is announced as the card attacks, as the legacy
  -- `keywordTriggers` case is. The stand is the `battleEnd` hook, run on the
  -- attacker at the Battle End Step after a guard's [Revenge]: while the card
  -- is still in play and has declared fewer than X attacks this turn — the
  -- one ending included — it switches to Active Mode (22-8-3). The legacy
  -- engine counts the stands granted (`extraAttacks`); this counts the
  -- attacks (`attacked`), which is the same number on a card that has
  -- attacked only with the keyword.
  at: [attacks]
  DO {}
  HOOK battleEnd {
    if(cond: all([inBattle(sel: [self], role: attacker), any([count([self] IN you.battle) >= 1, count([self] IN you.leader) >= 1]), NOT attacked(sel: [self], atLeast: $x)]), then: {
      switchMode(target: [self], mode: active)
    })
  }

-- 22-9
DEFINE KEYWORD Revenge
  TAKES ()
  text: "When this card becomes the guard card, KO the attacking card at the end of the battle."
  -- #156: two halves, as the legacy engine has them. The line answers
  -- `attacked` (`at:`), so it pends and is announced as the card becomes the
  -- guard — when it is attacked, or when it blocks — exactly as the legacy
  -- `keywordTriggers` case is; its `DO` has nothing of its own to do. The KO
  -- is the contract's own worked example, `HOOK battleEnd`, which
  -- `vm/battle.ts`'s Battle End Step fires on both cards of the fight — the
  -- body acts only on the one that is the guard then — after the combo cards
  -- have gone to the Drop and before
  -- `state.battle` clears — the legacy `battleCleanup` order. A Battle Card
  -- attacker only, as there (a Leader is not KO'd by it). The Revenge card
  -- need not survive the fight: a card KO'd by the battle still answers.
  at: [attacked]
  DO {}
  HOOK battleEnd {
    if(cond: all([inBattle(sel: [self], role: guard), count([attacker] IN opponent.battle) >= 1]), then: {
      ko(target: [attacker])
    })
  }

-- 22-12
DEFINE KEYWORD Indestructible
  TAKES ()
  text: "This card can't be KO'd or moved out of your Battle Area by the opponent's skills or as a result of battle."
  -- #154: the "as a result of battle" half is read directly in
  -- `vm/battle.ts`'s `damageWork`, not through this hook — a battle's own KO
  -- is not an effect's. A skill's KO is real since #146 (`vm/host.ts`), and
  -- the shared interpreter's `ko` case skips an opponent's [Indestructible]
  -- card itself, before this hook is asked — see docs/arena-ruleset-spec.md §4.3.
  HOOK koByEffect {
    forbid(what: beKOdBySkill, side: opponent, until: game)
    forbid(what: beMovedBySkill, side: opponent, until: game)
  }

-- 22-16
DEFINE KEYWORD Barrier
  TAKES ()
  text: "This card can't be chosen by the skills of cards your opponent masters."
  HOOK chooseable {
    forbid(what: beChosen, side: opponent, until: game)
  }

-- 22-20
DEFINE KEYWORD Deflect
  TAKES ()
  text: "This card isn't affected by your opponent's [Counter: Play] skills. Valid in every area."
  -- #150: asked of the card being played when its [Counter: Play] window
  -- opens (`vm/battle.ts`'s `windowClosedBy`), read declaratively like every
  -- query hook — a forbid on activating a counter empties the window, the
  -- legacy `counterCandidates`' own first line.
  HOOK counterWindow {
    forbid(what: activateCounter, side: opponent, until: game)
  }

-- 22-39
DEFINE KEYWORD Unique
  TAKES ()
  text: "While a card with [Unique] is in play you can't play another card with the same name. If two are somehow in play at once, their master keeps one and drops the rest."
  -- #157: asked of every card in play when a play is checked
  -- (`vm/program.ts`'s `forbiddenBy`) — the rule is the in-play card's, and it
  -- refuses its master's declared play of a card with its name, as the legacy
  -- `canPlay`/`whyNotPlay` do; a play a skill makes is not refused here, as it
  -- is not there. 21-11's half — two in play at once, the master keeps one —
  -- is rule processing, which the rules engine does not run yet.
  HOOK playRefused {
    forbid(what: play, side: you, sameNameAsSelf: true, bySkill: false, until: game)
  }

-- 22-40
DEFINE KEYWORD Servant
  TAKES ()
  text: "+10000 power, and the card does not switch to Active Mode during its master's Charge Phase."
  -- #154 (hook group A) builds the power half (attrBonus); #155 (hook
  -- group B) the Charge Phase half (activeStep).
  HOOK attrBonus {
    modifyAttr(target: [self], attr: power, amount: 10000)
  }
  HOOK activeStep {
    forbid(what: switchToActive, until: game)
  }

-- 22-31
DEFINE KEYWORD "Energy-Exhaust"
  TAKES ()
  text: "When this card is placed in an Energy Area, it arrives in Rest Mode. Valid in every area."
  HOOK chargeLimit {
    modifyAttr(target: [self], attr: mode, mode: rest)
  }

-- 22-18
DEFINE KEYWORD "Victory Strike"
  TAKES ()
  text: "Deal life damage by attacking with this card and you win the game."
  -- #156: the same hook: once its life damage has landed (and its moments
  -- fired) the game ends in its master's favour (22-18-2), and against a
  -- Unison guard it takes every marker (13-5-2-2), as on the legacy engine.
  HOOK beforeDamage {
    battleDamage(allMarkers: true, wins: true)
  }

-- 22-19
DEFINE KEYWORD "Warrior of Universe 7"
  TAKES ()
  text: "Treat your ≪Universe 7≫ cards in every area as having no specified cost — the coloured part of a play's price."
  -- Stage 7 (#153–#157)

-- 22-14
DEFINE KEYWORD Ultimate
  TAKES ()
  text: "A deck may hold at most one card with [Ultimate], and a card with it that leaves play is removed from the game rather than going anywhere else."
  -- #156 looked and left it unwritten. 22-14-3 is a replacement (9-10): the
  -- card leaving play or a Combo Area for anywhere but another of those goes
  -- to `removed` *instead* — one move, and the moments of that move, as the
  -- legacy `move` folds it into 14-1-4's Z-card line (printed keyword only;
  -- the cards under it are not redirected). `onLeave` cannot say it: it is an
  -- effect hook, run after the card has landed, so a body there would log a
  -- second move and fire the Drop's moments (`koed`) first. It needs a
  -- leave-time query — `onLeave` read declaratively before `moveCard` picks
  -- the zone, with a leaf naming the destination — or the 9-10 replacements
  -- `vm/host.ts`'s `replacementsFor` does not collect yet. The deck limit is
  -- `legality`'s, on both engines.

-- 22-17
DEFINE KEYWORD "Super Combo"
  TAKES ()
  text: "A deck may hold at most four cards with [Super Combo], counted across all of them."
  -- Stage 7 (#153–#157)

-- 22-28
DEFINE KEYWORD "Dragon Ball"
  TAKES ()
  text: "As many copies of a [Dragon Ball] card as you like, as long as no more than seven [Dragon Ball] cards are in the deck all told."
  -- #155: no body to write — a deck-building rule (`legality`), which no game
  -- reads on either engine.

-- 22-24
DEFINE KEYWORD Wormhole
  TAKES ()
  text: "[Over Realm] and [Dark Over Realm] may be activated twice a turn between them instead of once."
  -- #155 left it with [Over Realm]: its only effect is that keyword's limit,
  -- and [Over Realm] is unwritten (a counted, shared once-a-turn player
  -- attribute, above).

-- 22-37
DEFINE KEYWORD Invoker
  TAKES ()
  text: "A Red/Blue multicolour Extra Card in your hand may be activated by switching one active Red/Blue multicolour energy to Rest Mode instead of paying its energy cost."
  -- #155 looked and moved it to the payment hooks: an alternative price on an
  -- Extra's activation is the `altPayment` channel (hook group D), and
  -- `DEFINE ACTION activate` declares no `alt:`, `vm/costs.ts`' `altCostFor`
  -- reads no `altPayment` body and `payAltCost` has no `invoker` case.

-- 22-35
DEFINE KEYWORD Heroic
  TAKES ()
  text: "When you play another card with [Heroic], draw 1 card; the skill is then negated on this card for the rest of the turn."
  -- The "negated on this card for the rest of the turn" half is not built: a
  -- hook body's frame carries no skillIndex for `negate(what: own)` to read
  -- (`vm/program.ts`'s `hookFrame`), so this fires once per other [Heroic]
  -- card played in the turn rather than once. Named, not guessed around.
  HOOK afterSkill {
    if(cond: count("card with [Heroic]" FROM $source) >= 1, then: {
      draw(n: 1)
    })
  }

-- 22-36
DEFINE KEYWORD Villainous
  TAKES ()
  text: "When you play another card with [Villainous], your opponent chooses a card in their hand and drops it; the skill is then negated for the rest of the turn."
  -- Same gap as [Heroic]'s own HOOK: fires every time, not once a turn.
  HOOK afterSkill {
    if(cond: count("card with [Villainous]" FROM $source) >= 1, then: {
      choose(sel: 1 IN opponent.hand, chooser: opponent, as: "t")
      moveTo(target: $t, to: drop)
    })
  }

-- 22-33
DEFINE KEYWORD Offering
  TAKES ()
  text: "When this Battle Card is played, your opponent may put one of their life cards in their Drop Area. If they don't, you draw 2 cards."
  -- A whole-keyword activation that answers a moment (`at:`): the line pends
  -- at `played` as an [Auto] whose record said so would, and its `DO` runs as
  -- it resolves. The question is the opponent's, worded as the legacy
  -- engine's own `offering` prompt words its two answers, and the life card
  -- that goes is the top one, as it is there; with no life left there is
  -- nothing to ask and the draw simply happens (the legacy engine's own
  -- shortcut). One difference, recorded rather than matched: the question
  -- is the general `chooseMode` prompt here, not a prompt kind of its own.
  at: [played]
  DO {
    if(cond: count(IN opponent.life) >= 1, then: {
      chooseMode(modes: ["Drop 1 life (deny the draw)" {
        moveTo(target: TOP 1 IN opponent.life, to: drop, reveal: true)
      }, "Keep life (opponent draws 2)" {
        draw(n: 2)
      }], reason: "[Offering]: drop 1 life, or your opponent draws 2", chooser: opponent)
    }, else: {
      draw(n: 2)
    })
  }

-- 22-5
DEFINE KEYWORD Evolve
  TAKES (variant: string)
  text: "From hand: pay the cost, choose one of your Battle Cards matching the printed description, and play this card on top of it. [Xeno-Evolve] sends the chosen card to the Warp instead of stacking onto it."
  -- A move (#157), offered as an [Activate: Main] used from the hand (22-5-2)
  -- while a Battle Card matching the printed description is out — `asPrinted`
  -- reads "<V1>" off the line, the legacy `parseFilter(sk.effect || sk.cost)`.
  -- The price is the line's printed orbs. "when you use this card's [Evolve]
  -- from your hand" is the move's `keywordActivated(from: hand)`. The stack
  -- keeps the host's place, mode and power effects (`play … onto`,
  -- `vm/play.ts`'s `stackOnto`). [Xeno-Evolve] sends the host to the Warp and
  -- plays this card beside where it was (22-5-6).
  offer: "activate:main"
  REFUSE zone(area: hand) UNLESS count([self] IN you.hand) >= 1
  REFUSE target(reason: "no {line} in your Battle Area") UNLESS count(IN you.battle asPrinted) >= 1
  label: "{variant} {card} onto a {line}"
  DO {
    choose(sel: 1 IN you.battle asPrinted, as: "base", reason: "[Evolve]: choose the card to evolve")
    if(cond: oneOf(value: $variant, of: ["Xeno-Evolve"]), then: {
      moveTo(target: $base, to: warp)
      play(target: [self])
    }, else: {
      play(target: [self], onto: $base)
    })
  }

-- 22-13
DEFINE KEYWORD Union
  TAKES (variant: string)
  text: "Three ways to play a Battle Card by naming characters. Fusion drops one of each named character from your hand, both of equal power. Potara plays this card on top of two named characters in your Battle Area. Absorb is activated from the Battle Area, and its text says which card is played onto this one."
  -- A move (#157), one declaration for its three variants, told apart by
  -- `oneOf(value: $variant, …)`. Fusion and Potara are used from the hand and
  -- need each character the line names in ‹…› on a different card
  -- (`eachNamed`) — in the hand, of one power, for Fusion (22-13-4); in the
  -- Battle Area for Potara (22-13-5). Absorb is used from the Battle Area
  -- (22-13-6-2) and its `DO` does nothing of its own: the line's printed
  -- effect, which runs after the `DO` of every keyword move, is what says
  -- which card is played onto this one. "when you activate a [Union] skill"
  -- and "when this card's [Union-Absorb] is activated" are the move's
  -- `keywordActivated` under both names.
  offer: "activate:main"
  REFUSE zone(area: battle) UNLESS any([NOT oneOf(value: $variant, of: ["Absorb"]), count([self] IN you.battle) >= 1])
  REFUSE zone(area: hand) UNLESS any([oneOf(value: $variant, of: ["Absorb"]), count([self] IN you.hand) >= 1])
  REFUSE target(reason: "needs {names} in hand") UNLESS any([NOT oneOf(value: $variant, of: ["Fusion"]), eachNamed(sel: IN you.hand otherThanSelf)])
  REFUSE target(reason: "the two cards must have equal power") UNLESS any([NOT oneOf(value: $variant, of: ["Fusion"]), eachNamed(sel: IN you.hand otherThanSelf, samePower: true)])
  REFUSE target(reason: "needs {names} in your Battle Area") UNLESS any([NOT oneOf(value: $variant, of: ["Potara"]), eachNamed(sel: IN you.battle)])
  label: "Union-{variant} {card}"
  DO {
    if(cond: oneOf(value: $variant, of: ["Fusion"]), then: {
      choose(sel: 2 IN you.hand otherThanSelf asPrinted, as: "pair", reason: "[Union-Fusion]: choose the named cards to drop")
      moveTo(target: $pair, to: drop, cause: cost)
      play(target: [self])
    })
    if(cond: oneOf(value: $variant, of: ["Potara"]), then: {
      choose(sel: 1 IN you.battle asPrinted, as: "first", reason: "[Union-Potara]: choose the card to play this one onto")
      play(target: [self], onto: $first)
      choose(sel: 1 IN you.battle otherThanSelf asPrinted, as: "second", reason: "[Union-Potara]: choose the card to put under it")
      moveTo(target: $second, to: under, under: [self])
    })
  }

-- 22-15, 22-23
DEFINE KEYWORD "Over Realm"
  TAKES (x: number, dark: boolean)
  text: "With X or more cards in your Drop Area — X or more black cards, for the dark one — send your whole Drop Area to the Warp as the cost and play this card from hand. The two share one activation a turn. A card played with [Over Realm] goes to the Warp at the end of that turn."
  -- #157 looked and left it unwritten: its play goes through a [Counter: Play]
  -- window, which only a declared play opens today (`vm/battle.ts`'s
  -- `openPlayCounterWindow`), and "one activation a turn between them, two
  -- with [Wormhole]" is a counted player attribute (`playerAttr` reads
  -- booleans only). docs/arena-ruleset-spec.md §4.4.

-- 22-22
DEFINE KEYWORD Swap
  TAKES (x: number)
  text: "Return this Battle Card to your hand and play a named Battle Card with an energy cost of X from your hand in its place."
  -- #157 looked and left it unwritten: the chosen card is played through a
  -- [Counter: Play] window (as [Over Realm]'s is), and "an energy cost of X"
  -- is a parameter inside a card filter, which the filter grammar has no
  -- slot for. docs/arena-ruleset-spec.md §4.4.

-- 22-29
DEFINE KEYWORD Arrival
  TAKES (colors: colors)
  text: "During a battle, when the original colours of the Battle Cards in your Combo Area cover every colour named, pay the cost and play this card from hand."
  -- #155: a move, offered as an [Activate: Battle] at the combo prompt
  -- (22-29-4) from the hand, once the cards in your Combo Area carry every
  -- colour it names between them (`covers`, 22-29-3). The price is the line's
  -- printed orbs; the effect is the play itself (22-29-5), through the
  -- [Counter: Play] window a declared play opens, as on the legacy engine.
  offer: "activate:battle"
  REFUSE zone(area: hand) UNLESS count([self] IN you.hand) >= 1
  REFUSE condition(text: "{colors:and} Battle Cards in your Combo Area") UNLESS covers(sel: IN you.combo, colors: $colors)
  label: "Arrival {colors}: play {card}"
  DO {
    play(target: [self], counterWindow: true)
  }

-- 22-30
DEFINE KEYWORD Aegis
  TAKES (colors: colors)
  text: "In the Defense Step of your opponent's turn, drop cards from your hand covering the named colours to switch up to two of your energy from Rest to Active Mode."
  -- #154: a move, offered as an [Activate: Battle] at the combo prompt — so
  -- only in a battle, and the one the non-turn player is asked is the
  -- Defense Step's (22-30-4) — from a card in play, while the hand can cover
  -- the colours (`covers`), for the line's printed orbs, as the legacy
  -- `activatable` case gates it. Paying first, then up to two cards of the
  -- colours one at a time (the legacy prompt's `max` is the colours named,
  -- and every [Aegis] names two); cards that cover them go to the Drop as the
  -- cost (22-30-3), then up to two rested energy stand (22-30-5) and the
  -- combo prompt is put again. Picked wrongly, the orbs are spent and nothing
  -- happens, as there.
  offer: "activate:battle"
  REFUSE timing(window: defense) UNLESS all([isTurnPlayer(who: opponent), asking(prompt: combo)])
  REFUSE zone(area: battle) UNLESS count([self] IN you.play) >= 1
  REFUSE condition(text: "{colors:and} cards in your hand to drop") UNLESS covers(sel: IN you.hand, colors: $colors)
  label: "Aegis {colors}: drop {colors:and} from hand, stand up to 2 energy"
  DO {
    choose(sel: UP TO 2 (colors = $colors) IN you.hand, as: "cost", reason: "[Aegis]: drop cards covering the named colours from your hand")
    if(cond: covers(sel: FROM $cost, colors: $colors), then: {
      moveTo(target: $cost, to: drop, cause: cost)
      choose(sel: UP TO 2 IN you.energy rest, as: "stood", reason: "[Aegis]: energy to switch to Active Mode")
      switchMode(target: $stood, mode: active)
    }, else: {
      note(text: "Aegis: the cards dropped did not cover the colours, so nothing happened")
    })
  }

-- 22-32
DEFINE KEYWORD Alliance
  TAKES (colors: colors)
  text: "When this card attacks, you may switch one or more of your other Battle Cards of the named colours to Rest Mode as the cost of the printed effect."
  -- #154: a moment (`at:`), pended and announced as the card attacks, like
  -- the legacy `keywordTriggers` case; a condition printed before the colon
  -- is asked before anyone is asked anything. While the card is the
  -- attacker, its owner picks any number of their other active Battle Cards
  -- of the named colours, or none (22-32-3); those are rested as the cost,
  -- and only then is the printed effect announced and run, with the rested
  -- cards bound as `rested` — "the total power of the cards switched to Rest
  -- Mode by this skill" reads them (`printedEffect`). Declined, nothing
  -- happens. The legacy engine also pends "when this card is switched to
  -- Rest Mode by an [Alliance] skill" on each rested card; this engine fires
  -- no `modeSwitched` moment that says what did the switching (`by:`), so
  -- that trigger, like `restedBySkill`, does not answer here yet.
  at: [attacks]
  DO {
    if(cond: inBattle(sel: [self], role: attacker), then: {
      choose(sel: UP TO 99 (colors = $colors) IN you.battle active otherThanSelf, as: "rested", reason: "[Alliance]: Battle Cards to switch to Rest Mode, or none")
      if(cond: count(FROM $rested) >= 1, then: {
        switchMode(target: $rested, mode: rest)
        printedEffect()
      })
    })
  }

-- 22-34
DEFINE KEYWORD Revive
  TAKES (colors: colors)
  text: "When this Battle Card is KO'd, drop cards from hand whose original colours cover both named colours to play it back from your Drop Area. [Revive] is then negated on it for the turn."
  -- #155: a moment (`at:`), pended as the card is KO'd, like the legacy
  -- `keywordTriggers` case. Asked only while the card is still in the Drop
  -- and the hand can cover both colours (`covers`); the owner picks up to two
  -- cards of those colours (`colors = $colors`) or none (22-34-3). Cards that
  -- cover both go to the Drop as the cost, and the card is played back
  -- through the [Counter: Play] window (22-34-4). The legacy engine remembers
  -- the revival for the rest of the turn; here [Revive] is negated on the
  -- card for the turn, as 22-34-4 says, so a second KO that turn pends
  -- nothing — where the legacy engine announces the skill and does nothing.
  at: [koed]
  DO {
    if(cond: all([count([self] IN you.drop) >= 1, covers(sel: IN you.hand, colors: $colors)]), then: {
      choose(sel: UP TO 2 (colors = $colors) IN you.hand, as: "cost", reason: "[Revive]: drop cards covering both colours to play this card back, or none")
      if(cond: count(FROM $cost) >= 1, then: {
        if(cond: all([covers(sel: FROM $cost, colors: $colors), count([self] IN you.drop) >= 1]), then: {
          moveTo(target: $cost, to: drop, cause: cost)
          negateOwnSkill(until: turn)
          play(target: [self], counterWindow: true)
        }, else: {
          note(text: "Revive: the cards chosen did not cover the colours, so it stays in the Drop")
        })
      })
    })
  }

-- 22-38
DEFINE KEYWORD Successor
  TAKES ()
  text: "Drop any number of mono-green, mono-yellow or Green/Yellow Battle Cards from your Battle Area whose energy costs add up to exactly this card's printed cost, and play it from hand."
  -- #155: a move, offered as an [Activate: Main] from the hand while the
  -- green/yellow cards in your Battle Area can make the card's energy cost
  -- exactly (`sumsTo`, 22-38-2). The cards are picked one at a time, and only
  -- those that still leave a way to the exact sum are offered (`choose …
  -- sumTo`, the legacy `successorAsk`); they go to the Drop as the cost and
  -- the card is played through the [Counter: Play] window (22-38-3/4). The
  -- price is the line's printed orbs.
  offer: "activate:main"
  REFUSE zone(area: hand) UNLESS count([self] IN you.hand) >= 1
  REFUSE target(reason: "no green/yellow Battle Cards adding up to its energy cost") UNLESS sumsTo(sel: (colors = [Green, Yellow] AND notColors = [Red, Blue, Black, White, Colorless]) IN you.battle, attr: energyCost, total: attr([self], energyCost))
  label: "Successor: play {card} by dropping green/yellow Battle Cards"
  DO {
    choose(sel: (colors = [Green, Yellow] AND notColors = [Red, Blue, Black, White, Colorless]) IN you.battle, as: "paid", reason: "[Successor]: green/yellow Battle Cards to drop", sumTo: attr([self], energyCost))
    if(cond: count(FROM $paid) >= 1, then: {
      moveTo(target: $paid, to: drop, cause: cost)
      play(target: [self], counterWindow: true)
    })
  }

-- 22-41
DEFINE KEYWORD Overlord
  TAKES ()
  text: "Put one of your Battle Cards with [Servant] at the bottom of your deck as the cost, and draw 1 card."
  -- A whole-keyword activation that is a move (`offer:`): the line is an
  -- [Activate: Main] in every sense the `activate` paragraph's gates read
  -- (negation, 20-14, the window), plus the one requirement 22-41-2 adds.
  -- The card that pays is chosen; with one [Servant] in play that choice is
  -- forced and taken without a question, and with several the player picks —
  -- 22-41-2 says "one of your Battle Cards", where the legacy engine takes
  -- the first. "when you activate an [Overlord] skill" is the move's
  -- `keywordActivated` moment (`triggers.rules`' `overlordActivated`).
  offer: "activate:main"
  REFUSE target(reason: "no [Servant] in your Battle Area") UNLESS count("card with [Servant]" IN you.battle) >= 1
  REFUSE zone(area: battle) UNLESS count([self] IN you.battle) >= 1
  label: "Overlord: return a Servant to the deck, draw 1"
  DO {
    choose(sel: 1 "card with [Servant]" IN you.battle, as: "servant", reason: "[Overlord]: the [Servant] to put at the bottom of your deck")
    moveTo(target: $servant, to: deck, position: bottom, cause: cost)
    draw(n: 1)
  }

-- 22-42
DEFINE KEYWORD Rejuvenate
  TAKES ()
  text: "A Unison Card with cards beneath it: drop one of them and pay the skill cost, then add the top card of your deck to your life."
  -- #155 looked and left it unwritten: its price ("Remove N markers from this
  -- card") is printed as the line's text, which the record reads as an effect,
  -- so the 13-4 gates (enough markers, one marker skill a turn) have no number
  -- to read. The order is sayable — DO drops the card from beneath, the
  -- printed effect removes the markers, AFTER adds the life — the gate is not.

-- 22-43
DEFINE KEYWORD "Spirit Boost"
  TAKES (x: number)
  text: "Part of a skill's cost: remove X markers from your Unison Card. A skill whose [Spirit Boost] can't be paid can't be activated."
  -- #157: no body — a price, not a move or a hook. `DEFINE COST spiritBoost`
  -- (costs.rules) is what paying it does, and the `activate` paragraph's COST
  -- names it; the activation binds X off the line's tag.

-- 22-45
DEFINE KEYWORD Empower
  TAKES (color: color, x: number)
  text: "When you play this Unison Card over one whose colour matches, you may move up to Y markers from the Unison being replaced onto this one. An [Empower] naming no colour takes them from a Unison of any colour."
  -- #157 looked and left it unwritten: the carry is a question asked in the
  -- middle of a play, before the replaced Unison leaves, and the `play` op
  -- cannot suspend for an answer; the markers paid for the Unison are a later
  -- step of `playUnison`'s DO here, so the carry belongs to that move rather
  -- than to `play`. docs/arena-ruleset-spec.md §4.4.

-- 22-46
DEFINE KEYWORD "Z-Awaken"
  TAKES ()
  text: "From the Z-Deck, once a turn: pay the Z-Energy cost and the skill cost and place this Z-Leader on top of your already-awakened Leader, which has to match the printed description. The stack is one card from then on."
  -- #155 looked and left it unwritten: a stack onto the Leader Area carrying
  -- the old Leader's power effects and battle role (`stackOnto` knows the
  -- Battle Area), a Z-Energy price on a keyword move, and a once-a-turn
  -- counter per player — none of which the language or `vm/` has yet.

-- 22-47
DEFINE KEYWORD "Z-Stack"
  TAKES (x: number)
  text: "When this Z-Card is placed on your Leader or into a Battle or Unison Area, put up to X cards matching the printed description from your Z-Deck underneath it. They become part of the card on top."
  -- #155: a moment (`at:`), pended as the card is played and as it is placed
  -- on the Leader, like the legacy `keywordTriggers` case. The candidates are
  -- the Z-Deck cards the line's description matches (`asPrinted`), up to X of
  -- them or none. One difference, recorded rather than copied: each card goes
  -- straight under (23-2), where the legacy engine logs a move to the Battle
  -- Area first and then lifts it out of the area again.
  at: [played, leaderPlaced]
  DO {
    choose(sel: UP TO $x IN you.zDeck asPrinted, as: "stack", reason: "[Z-Stack]: cards from your Z-Deck to place under this card")
    moveTo(target: $stack, to: under, under: [self])
  }
